        reviewedAt = "2026-11-13",
        itemId = 104208,
        name = "Spawn of Galakras",
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/item=104208",
        mountCategory = "Achievements",
        stepCount = 16,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Group passing, two separate Spoils teams, Thok's health-triggered phase and repeated Paragon mantles.\n\n1. Enter Siege of Orgrimmar on Normal or higher in the Vale (74.0,42.0), track 8454 and agree on the missing criteria before pulling. Normal is sufficient for this mount meta; Mythic-only Kor'kron Juggernaut is a different reward.\n\n2. At Immerseus, bring him to a split, then root/stun hostile Sha Puddles so they cannot reach the centre. When they become Tears of the Vale, kill them. Repeat until ten Tears have died before finishing the encounter; do not instantly kill every puddle.\n\n3. At Fallen Protectors, lower Rook to a Desperate Measures phase without killing the encounter. Spread the passing group into a long chain and transfer Mark of Anguish through at least five unique players, totalling at least 200 yards in that ONE phase. Six spaced players and coordinated near-maximum-range throws make the distance easier to verify. Then finish the fight.\n\n4. At Norushen, kill the Amalgam without any Unleashed Corruption reaching it; a direct high-level kill before adds spawn works. At Sha of Pride, kill quickly without anyone receiving Pride from Manifestations while Norushen is alive; avoid killing a manifestation beside unprotected players.\n\n5. At Galakras, protect ALL friendly NPCs, including the tower demolition crew, through the waves. Clear the opened tower, use its cannon to shoot Galakras down and finish him. Leaving the friendly leaders or crew unguarded can fail The Immortal Vanguard.\n\n6. At Iron Juggernaut, wait for Siege Mode. Kite Cutter Laser through Crawler Mines to superheat them, then click/stomp six superheated mines before killing the boss. Normal mines do not count. Manage the launch/fall damage between stomps.\n\n7. Before the Dark Shaman, rescue Ji Firepaw by killing his captor, obtain the bank guard's prison key and free occupied prisoners, and free a group of unwilling fighters by killing their captors with single-target attacks. Keep the neutral prisoners alive, then defeat the shaman.\n\n8. Clear Nazgrim's approach without starting the boss. Release Gamon from his chains, escort him into the room and defeat Nazgrim with Gamon alive and participating. Do not pull the boss before he arrives.\n\n9. Before Malkorok, preserve the Corrupted Skullsplitter near the stairs. Bring it into the boss room and put it in Breath of Y'Shaarj so it transforms into a Corrupted Amalgamation; the breath must actually hit it. Then finish the required enemies and Malkorok.\n\n10. At Spoils, assign separate Mogu-only and Mantid-only teams. Each player must kill only their assigned enemy family for the entire encounter. At the midpoint swap sides so each team continues on the SAME family in the next room; coordinate both levers. Two players can do the split, but uncontrolled pets/AoE across families can ruin Criss Cross.\n\n11. At Thok, use the lowest practical raid size and have at least five players enter his bloodied threshold together to trigger the frenzy transition; a high-level character standing at full health may never trigger it. Prepare controlled health-lowering effects and avoid healing the group prematurely. Kill jailers for keys and use three keys on the Thrice-Locked snail cage rather than spending them all on ordinary prisoner cages.\n\n12. Once the snail cage opens, keep everyone out of the snail's path and kill Thok. Let the snail reach and eat the corpse before leaving; opening the cage alone is not the achievement.\n\n13. At Siegecrafter, keep the four conveyor weapon categories undestroyed across your credited kills: laser, missile, electromagnet and crawler mines. At high level, killing Blackfuse before destroying any conveyor weapons is the straightforward way to satisfy all four restrictions.\n\n14. At the Paragons, click a dead Paragon whose power your current role can take BEFORE ending the encounter. Finish the fight to register the mantle. Repeat on separate eligible Normal/Heroic/Mythic fights or later weeks with two other compatible mantles; the same mantle three times does not count. You need three different mantles, not every listed mantle.\n\n15. At Garrosh, keep eighteen Kor'kron Warbringers alive and gather them in one Iron Star lane. Let ONE Iron Star kill all eighteen, confirm Strike!'s counter, then defeat Garrosh. Do not AoE the waves down or finish phase one before enough adds are present.\n\n16. Review all fourteen 8454 criteria before leaving. Complete any missing setup on another eligible difficulty/reset, then learn Reins of Galakras from bags/mail or check the automatic Mount Journal reward.",
    },
